   "daf": "78b",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "הָהוּא דַּאֲמַר לְהוּ: אַבְזְקָת בְּמֵילָתָא דְּמַלְכָּא, אֲמַרוּ לֵיהּ: בְּמַאי? בְּטַלֵּי כְסַף, אוֹ בְּטַלֵּי דְהַב? אִיכָּא דְּאָמְרִי: בְּטַלֵּי כְסַף אֲמַר, וְקַטְלוּהּ. אִיכָּא דְּאָמְרִי: בְּטַלֵּי דְהַב אֲמַר, וְשַׁבְקוּהּ.",
   "en": "With regard to the term worm rot, the Gemara relates: There was «a certain» individual «who said to» others: I saw «worm rot on the king’s clothing. They said to him: On what» did you see it? «On silver,» i.e., linen, «items or on gold,» i.e., woolen, «items? There are» those «who say» that «he said» he had seen it «on silver items, and they killed him.» Since worms are not found on linen garments, they realized that he must have been lying. «There are» those «who say» that «he said» he had seen it «on gold items, and» therefore «they let him be.»"
  }
 ],
